# Placeholders to be replaced

## 1. GPIO Pin Configuration (Core/Src/UserTask.cpp, line ~24-29)
**Current placeholder pins:**
```cpp
LineFollower::SensorPins line_follower_pins = {
    GPIOB, GPIO_PIN_12,  // Slot sensor (placeholder: LED1)
    GPIOB, GPIO_PIN_13,  // Left sensor (placeholder: LED2)
    GPIOC, GPIO_PIN_13,  // Middle sensor (placeholder: BTN_0)
    GPIOC, GPIO_PIN_14   // Right sensor (placeholder: BTN_1)
};
```

**Action required:**
- Configure actual IR sensor GPIO pins in STM32CubeMX
- Update the pin assignments in UserTask.cpp:
  - slot_port_ and slot_pin_ → Actual slot detection sensor pin
  - left_port_ and left_pin_ → Actual left IR sensor pin
  - middle_port_ and middle_pin_ → Actual middle IR sensor pin
  - right_port_ and right_pin_ → Actual right IR sensor pin

**Example replacement:**
```cpp
LineFollower::SensorPins line_follower_pins = {
    GPIOA, GPIO_PIN_0,   // Slot sensor
    GPIOA, GPIO_PIN_1,   // Left sensor
    GPIOA, GPIO_PIN_2,   // Middle sensor
    GPIOA, GPIO_PIN_3    // Right sensor
};
```

## 2. Motor Control Interface (Core/Src/UserTask.cpp, line ~85-89)
**Current placeholder:**
```cpp
LineFollower::MotorCommand cmd = g_line_follower.getMotorCommand();
(void)cmd;  // Suppress unused variable warning until motor interface is implemented

// TODO: 调用实际的电机控制接口
// motor_controller.setSpeed(cmd.left_speed, cmd.right_speed);
```

**Action required:**
- Implement or integrate with existing wheel PID controller
- Replace the TODO comment with actual motor control function call
- cmd.left_speed and cmd.right_speed range: -1024 to 1024
- 0 = stop, 1024 = full speed forward

**Example replacement:**
```cpp
LineFollower::MotorCommand cmd = g_line_follower.getMotorCommand();
// Call actual motor controller (example interface)
motor_controller.setLeftSpeed(cmd.left_speed);
motor_controller.setRightSpeed(cmd.right_speed);
// OR if using differential drive:
// motor_controller.setDifferentialSpeed(cmd.left_speed, cmd.right_speed);
```


## 3. Target Slot from Vision System (Not yet implemented)
**Current status:** 
- Line follower reads sensors and follows line
- Slot detection sensor (S) is read but not used for logic
- No integration with vision system for target slot number

**Action required when implementing slot detection (Feature #2):**
- Get target slot number from vision UART module
- Implement slot counting in LineFollowerController
- Stop at target slot when S sensor detects junction
- Suggested interface in LineFollowerController:
  ```cpp
  void setTargetSlot(uint8_t _target_slot);  // 1-4
  bool isAtTargetSlot();  // Check if arrived
  ```


## 4. Calibration Constants (Core/Modules/line_follower.hpp, line ~79-81)
**Current values (may need tuning):**
```cpp
constexpr int16_t NOMINAL_SPEED = 1024;           // Base speed
constexpr float GENTLE_TURN_RATIO = 0.7f;         // Gentle turn reduction
constexpr float SHARP_TURN_RATIO = 0.3f;          // Sharp turn reduction
constexpr uint32_t LINE_FOLLOWER_UPDATE_RATE_MS = 20;  // 50Hz
```

**Action required:**
- Test on actual robot and tune these values for:
  - Optimal speed without losing line
  - Smooth vs. responsive turning
  - Update rate based on sensor sampling and motor response time


## 5. Sensor Polarity (Core/Modules/line_follower.cpp, line ~54-58)
**Current assumption:**
- GPIO_PIN_SET (HIGH) = line detected (dark line)
- GPIO_PIN_RESET (LOW) = no line (light surface)

**Action required if sensor logic is inverted:**
- Test actual IR sensor output when over black line
- If inverted, change line 56-59 in line_follower.cpp:
  ```cpp
  // If HIGH = no line, LOW = line detected:
  readings.left = (HAL_GPIO_ReadPin(pins_.left_port_, pins_.left_pin_) == GPIO_PIN_RESET) ? 1 : 0;
  ```
